  "decision": "revise",
  "reasoning": "The plan mostly aligns with the intended shape: issues is scanned first via PRIMARY in reverse order to satisfy ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 10 without a sort, projects is joined by a single-row PRIMARY lookup (eq_ref-like), and enabled_modules is probed per outer row via an index lookup (not materialized). However, the NOT IN subquery against members was transformed into an <in_optimizer> check backed by a materialized deduplicated subquery that is computed once and then consulted per row. This contradicts the objective/expected evidence that required the members subquery to be evaluated dependently (e.g., DEPENDENT SUBQUERY or index_subquery) with no materialization.",
  "query_assessments": [
    {
      "query_id": "calibration_query_1",
      "sql": "SELECT /*+ SET_VAR(optimizer_switch='semijoin=off,materialization=off,in_to_exists=on') */ issues.* FROM issues FORCE INDEX (PRIMARY) STRAIGHT_JOIN projects ON projects.id = issues.project_id WHERE (((projects.status <> 9 AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 AS one FROM enabled_modules em WHERE em.project_id = projects.id AND em.name = 'issue_tracking')) AND (((projects.is_public = 1 AND projects.id NOT IN (SELECT project_id FROM members WHERE user_id IN (44, 638)) AND ((issues.is_private = 0 OR issues.author_id = 44 OR issues.assigned_to_id IN (44, 186, 898)))) ) OR (projects.id IN (1, 6, 9, 13, 115, 129, 131, 136, 186, 227, 228, 230, 275, 287, 315, 335, 340, 369, 394, 404, 408, 450, 453, 454, 456, 458, 460, 462, 492, 511, 512, 516, 519, 527, 531, 533, 537) AND ((issues.is_private = 0 OR issues.author_id = 44 OR issues.assigned_to_id IN (44, 186, 898)))) OR (projects.id IN (40, 68, 130, 149, 326, 330, 331, 332, 333, 350, 356, 402, 455, 514, 515, 528) AND (1 = 1)) OR (projects.id IN (91, 111, 128, 130, 149, 235, 257, 322, 326, 328, 330, 331, 332, 333, 350, 356, 489, 508, 514, 515, 525, 528) AND ((issues.is_private = 0 OR issues.author_id = 44 OR issues.assigned_to_id IN (44, 186, 898)))) OR (projects.id IN (457) AND ((issues.is_private = 0 OR issues.author_id = 44 OR issues.assigned_to_id IN (44, 186, 898)))))) AND (issues.id != 251880) AND (LOWER(issues.subject) LIKE LOWER('%255392%'))) ORDER BY issues.id DESC LIMIT 10",
      "matched": false,
      "observed_plan_summary": "Limit 10 over Nested loop: Index range scan on issues using PRIMARY (reverse) with filter including lower(subject) LIKE '%255392%'; per-row single-row lookup on enabled_modules via uq_enabled_modules; single-row PRIMARY lookup on projects; NOT IN(members) rewritten to <in_optimizer> with a deduplicated materialized subquery computed once and checked per-row.",
      "supporting_evidence": [
        "Index range scan on issues using PRIMARY (reverse); ORDER BY id DESC satisfied without sort",
        "Single-row index lookup on projects using PRIMARY (eq_ref-like)",
        "Enabled_modules probed per row: Single-row covering index lookup on em using uq_enabled_modules (project_id,name)"
      ],
      "discrepancies": [
        "Members NOT IN subquery was materialized: 'Materialize with deduplication' under <in_optimizer>; 'Select #3 (subquery in condition; run only once)' indicating non-dependent evaluation"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "revised_blueprint": {
    "incident_spec": {
      "dbms": "mysql",
      "dbms_version": null,
      "summary": "Slow query against large issues table with complex authorization predicates, EXISTS check, NOT EXISTS (members) anti-join, leading-wildcard LIKE on subject, and ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 10.",
      "symptoms": [
        "Single SELECT takes ~15 seconds",
        "EXPLAIN shows issues scanned with PRIMARY key range and Using where",
        "Correlated authorization checks add per-row cost when evaluated dependently"
      ],
      "mechanism": "Leading-wildcard LIKE on subject prevents index use and forces scanning many issues in descending PK order to find 10 matches; OR-heavy predicates and dependent EXISTS/NOT EXISTS checks add per-row CPU and
